The test vehicle approaches the intersection at target speed V1. Pedestrians waiting to cross the crosswalk are positioned on the left/right side of the current lane, with a distance D between them and the lane centerline. The pedestrian crosses the crosswalk from the left/right side of the current lane at speed V2. During the test vehicle's left turn through the intersection, the time required for the test vehicle to reach the collision point is identical to the time required for the pedestrian to reach the collision point.